        <span class="card__phase-label">Phase 03</span>
        <h2 class="card__heading">Context Engineering</h2>
        <p class="card__body">Output quality depends less on clever prompts than on richness of context: instructions, knowledge, memory, examples, tools, and guardrails. The boundary between static context (always loaded) and dynamic context (pulled on demand via Agent Skills) is a first-class architectural decision — too much static context wastes tokens, too little causes agents to forget critical rules.</p>
      </article>

